# Compact responsive layouts

Prefer horizontal, dense layouts over long vertical stacks.

## Grid breakpoints

- Mobile: 1 column
- Tablet (`md`): 2 columns
- Desktop/laptop (`lg`): 3 columns
- Large desktop (`xl`): 4 columns

Use: `grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 xl:grid-cols-4`

## Requirements

- Use CSS Grid or Flexbox; use full available width.
- Reduce unnecessary padding, margins, gaps, and control heights (`h-8` / `h-9`).
- Keep related form fields, filters, and actions on the same row when width allows.
- Display dashboard/KPI cards in multiple columns.
- Avoid unnecessary full-width components.
- Large tables: horizontal scroll (`forceTable` / `overflow-x-auto`), do not convert every row into stacked cards.
- Keep primary actions visible without excessive scrolling.
- Preserve readability, accessibility, responsiveness, and existing functionality.
